https://github.com/getzep/graphiti/blob/6c7752f15b3164335a9df27d1f3bc758129764de/graphiti_core/utils/bulk_utils.py#L193

Hi, here i think the type of the variable `existing_nodes_chunks` is `list[list[list[EntityNode]]]`. It causes some problems when calling `dedupe_extracted_nodes` because `existing_nodes_chunks[i]` is `list[list[EntityNode]]`, which does not match the signature of `dedupe_extracted_nodes` which expects a `list[EntityNode]` for the parameter `existing_nodes`. same in `dedupe_edges_bulk`.

```python
    results: list[tuple[list[EntityNode], dict[str, str]]] = list(
        await semaphore_gather(
            *[
                dedupe_extracted_nodes(llm_client, node_chunk, existing_nodes_chunks[i])
                for i, node_chunk in enumerate(node_chunks)
            ]
        )
    )
```

In my case I solved both by flattening but I don't know if this is the expected behavior for you.

```python
    existing_nodes_chunks: list[list[list[EntityNode]]] = list(
        await semaphore_gather(
            *[get_relevant_nodes(driver, node_chunk, SearchFilters()) for node_chunk in node_chunks]
        )
    )

    results: list[tuple[list[EntityNode], dict[str, str]]] = list(
        await semaphore_gather(
            *[
                dedupe_extracted_nodes(llm_client, node_chunk, [node for sublist in existing_nodes_chunks[i] for node in sublist])
                for i, node_chunk in enumerate(node_chunks)
            ]
        )
    )

```

